{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Moses wrote all the words of YHWH.</b> These are the conditions: ״והיה אם שמוע תשמעו בקולי ושמרתם את בריתי״ — 'And it shall be if you will surely hearken to My voice and keep My covenant,' etc. <br><b>And he rose early in the morning and built an altar under the mountain.</b> This was on the fifth of Sivan. <br><b>All the words which YHWH has spoken we will do.</b> Our Rabbi Hananel, of blessed memory, explained that נעשה ('we will do') is an inclusive commandment encompassing positive commandments and negative commandments, for one who refrains from doing a thing concerning which he was warned not to do it is called one who performed a commandment, since he fulfilled the warning with which he was charged. And a full verse it is (Psalms 119:3): ״אף לא פעלו עולה בדרכיו הלכו״ — 'They also do no iniquity; they walk in His ways' — Scripture explains that when they did not do iniquity, it is as though they walked in His ways."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:29.566558438Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}